data.content:
Here's the full program targeting `net11.0`:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase
};

var person = new Person("Alice", 30);
Console.WriteLine(JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options));

public record Person(string name, int age);
```

**Output:**
```json
{"Name":"Alice","Age":30}
```

`JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` is available out of the box in .NET 11's `System.Text.Json`. Since positional record parameters `string name, int age` generate lowercase properties (`name`, `age`), the PascalCase policy converts them to `Name` and `Age` in the JSON output.
